# Storybook (`packages/ui`)

See also **`storybook-ui-stories.mdc`** (generic canvas copy, footer colocation) and **`ui-atomic-architecture.mdc`** (which components live in which layer).

## Sidebar = `src/patterns`

- Do **not** set `title` on the story `meta` default export. Story names come from the file path under `packages/ui/src/patterns` (via `apps/storybook/.storybook/main.ts` `directory` → `patterns`).
- To change where a story appears, **move or rename the file/folders** under `patterns/` (e.g. `Atoms/`, `Molecules/`, `Organisms/`, `Templates/`). Do not invent path strings in code.
- Atom layout under `patterns/Atoms/` is **filesystem-driven** (sidebar mirrors folders). Current groups:
  - **`Branding/`**, **`Interactive/`**, **`Spatial/`** — primary buckets (no `*Atoms` suffix on these three).
  - **`DisplayAtoms/`**, **`LayoutAtoms/`**, **`EnvironmentalAtoms/`** — additional atom groupings (keep names aligned with real folders when adding stories).
  - Shared SCSS such as **`animations/`** may live alongside these; colocate stories only when a component warrants them.
- Do **not** add a top-level group like `Style Guide/` or other labels that are not real folder names under `patterns/`.
- Top-level sidebar order is fixed in `apps/storybook/.storybook/preview.ts` (`storySort`): Atoms → Molecules → Organisms → Templates.
- Per-component **Docs** tab content can use `parameters.docs.description` on story `meta` (see Primitives, Pairings, Typography). Standalone markdown-in-canvas “guide” stories are optional; do not add them without an agreed doc strategy.

## Hoisting / “redundant naming” (Storybook default)

- Storybook may **collapse** a folder and a single story file when their names match after normalization (often **case-insensitive**), e.g. `Alert/Alert.stories.tsx` can show as one row under `Molecules`. **This is normal** and acceptable for ReadBoot—do **not** rename stories to `component.stories.tsx` or other artificial stems unless you explicitly want an extra folder row in the sidebar.
- Prefer **natural** names: `ComponentName/ComponentName.stories.tsx` next to `ComponentName.tsx`.
- Folders with **multiple** story files (e.g. `Colors/Pairings.stories.tsx` and `Primitives.stories.tsx`) stay expanded as a group.

## ESLint

- `storybook/no-title-property-in-meta` is enabled for `@repo/ui` story files—do not add `title` to meta.

## Branding assets (SSOT)

- **Logo and favicon** live under `packages/ui/src/assets/branding/` (e.g. `readboot-logo.png`, `favicon.png`). The logo is always that asset where a logo is shown—do not substitute a different file for “the logo” in stories.
- **Story-only visuals** (e.g. a blog featured image mock) belong under `packages/ui/src/assets/storybook/` so they are clearly not brand marks.
- Storybook serves `packages/ui/src/assets` at `/assets/...` via `staticDirs` in `apps/storybook/.storybook/main.ts`. Manager `brandImage` and `preview-head` favicon use branding URLs.
- Do not use external placeholder image URLs in stories; use bundled paths under `/assets/...`.
- **Placeholder art** lives only in `packages/ui/src/assets/storybook/` and is **imported** from `@repo/ui` (see `placeholders.ts`). Next.js bundles those assets from the package; Storybook still maps `packages/ui/src/assets` at `/assets` for any raw URL usage. Do **not** duplicate placeholders under `apps/*/public/`. The ReadBoot **logo** stays under `assets/branding/` only.

## WordPress-shaped data & server-only components

- **Image URL strings in mocks** — When a WP type expects a **`sourceUrl` string** (e.g. `Post.featuredImage.node.sourceUrl`) but you import art from `assets/storybook/placeholders.ts`, use **`placeholderSrc(asset)`** so the same mock works under Next (`StaticImageData`) and Storybook/Vite (often a plain string). Do not hand-roll `.src` from `StaticImageData` in stories; reuse **`wpShowcaseMocks.ts`** for Showcase/BlogShowcase-shaped grids when possible.
- **Server / async RSC** — Default **`LogoImage`** (async, optional WP fetch) and **`BlogShowcase`** (async `getPosts`) are not executed in the Storybook canvas. Preview with **`LogoImageClient`**, **`Showcase` + `MOCK_POSTS` / `MOCK_PROJECTS`**, or document the real entry in **`parameters.docs.description`** (see existing `LogoImage.stories.tsx` and `BlogShowcase.stories.tsx`).

## Fonts (canvas parity)

- Match `apps/web/app/layout.tsx` Google Fonts in `apps/storybook/.storybook/preview-head.html`.
